      "math_academy_id": "q-74179",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that $‖2u+3v‖=31$ and $‖u‖=5$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+3v‖ & \\le ‖2u‖+‖3v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+3v‖ & \\le 2‖u‖+3‖v‖ \\\\ 31 & \\le 2\\cdot 5+3‖v‖ \\\\ 31 & \\le 10+3‖v‖ \\\\ 21 & \\le 3‖v‖ \\\\ 7 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $7.$",
